<h2><%= t("team_room.index.title", name: @team.name) %></h2>

<%# The roster, and nothing else. Every control that acts on the team used to
    sit in here interleaved with the members, so "Пригласить участников" read
    as though it were another name in the list, and the handover <select> --
    which inherits the global `select { width: 100% }` from components.css --
    spanned the whole card and cut the buttons into three unrelated-looking
    groups. %>
<fieldset class="card">
  <legend>
    <%= t("team_room.index.composition") %>
  </legend>

  <ul class="game-list">
  <% @team.members.each do |member| %>
    <li>
      <%= member.nickname %> <%= t("team_room.index.captain_suffix") if member.captain? %>
    </li>
  <% end %>
  </ul>
</fieldset>

<%# The controls, lifted out of the card above. Only the markup around them
    moved -- every visibility condition is unchanged, and each one still
    guards itself here rather than relying on the controller.

    Safe to regroup: the two frozen "Не капитан" scenarios in
    features/games/registration-to-game.feature assert page-WIDE that a
    non-captain sees neither "Подать заявку на регистрацию" nor a link
    "Отозвать" -- `не должен видеть`, with no `в блоке` scope -- so which
    fieldset a control sits in cannot affect them. What still matters is that
    no label here drifts towards either of those strings. %>
<div class="team-actions">
  <div class="team-actions__row">
    <% if @current_user.captain? %>
      <%= link_to t("team_room.index.invite"), new_invitation_path, class: "btn" %>
    <% end %>

    <%# Where a member goes to move somewhere else. Link text is deliberately
        unrelated to the game-registration strings above. %>
    <%= link_to t("team_room.index.browse_teams"), teams_path, class: "btn" %>

    <%# Hidden exactly where TeamsController#leave refuses, so it is never a
        promise that cannot be kept: mid-race (D1), and for a captain who
        still has teammates -- they see the handover control below instead,
        and once they have handed over, this appears. A solo captain may
        leave (D5), taking the role with them.

        button_to rather than form_with: there is nothing to select. %>
    <% unless @team.in_live_race? %>
      <% if !@current_user.captain? || @team.members.count == 1 %>
        <%= button_to t("team_room.index.leave"), leave_teams_path,
                      :method => :post, :class => "btn" %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# Captain-only, hidden mid-race (D1) and when the captain is the only
      member, since there would be nobody to hand to.

      A real form, not a link: this app ships no Turbo and no rails-ujs, so
      link_to with method: :post would silently issue a GET against a
      POST-only route.

      On its own line beneath the buttons, with the <select> next to the
      button that submits it. The field and its verb belong together, and a
      nickname reads better at its natural width than stretched across the
      page. %>
  <% if @current_user.captain? && !@team.in_live_race? %>
    <% candidates = @team.members.reject { |member| member.id == @current_user.id } %>
    <% if candidates.any? %>
      <%= form_with url: hand_over_team_path(@team), method: :post,
                    class: "team-actions__handover" do %>
        <%= select_tag :member_id,
                       options_from_collection_for_select(candidates, :id, :nickname) %>
        <%= submit_tag t("team_room.index.hand_over"), :class => "btn" %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# The captain's queue of people asking to join -- its own card now, rather
    than an <h3> inside the composition card. These are not members yet, and
    each row carries two controls of its own.

    Rendered only when the captain has something to decide: @join_requests is
    empty for everyone else, which is what keeps this clear of the frozen
    "Не капитан" scenarios. These labels match neither asserted string.

    Real forms, not links: no Turbo and no rails-ujs here.

    The captain? check is deliberately duplicated rather than left to
    TeamRoomController#index's decision to assign an empty list. Every other
    control on this page guards itself the same way, and a visibility rule
    that lives only in the controller leaks the moment a different caller
    renders this template. %>
<% if @current_user.captain? && @join_requests.any? %>
  <fieldset class="card">
    <legend>
      <%= t("team_room.index.join_requests") %>
    </legend>

    <ul class="game-list">
      <% @join_requests.each do |join_request| %>
        <li>
          <%= join_request.user.nickname %>
          <%= button_to t("team_room.index.accept_request"),
                        accept_join_request_path(join_request),
                        :method => :post, :class => "btn" %>
          <%= button_to t("team_room.index.reject_request"),
                        reject_join_request_path(join_request),
                        :method => :post, :class => "btn" %>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  </fieldset>
<% end %>

<%= render "shared/current_games" %>

<%= render "dashboard/coming_games" %>

<%= render "dashboard/finished_games" %>
